    "body": "# What does this PR do ?\r\n\r\nWith FP8 delayed scaling, we preemptively quantize the LoRA branch input to enable a fused RMSNorm + FP8 quant kernel and a [FP8 dropout+dequant kernel](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/pull/2014). However, this does not generalize to more modern recipes like MXFP8 and NVFP4, so this PR removes this optimization.\r\n\r\nPrevious FP8 path:\r\n```\r\n-> RMSNorm+quant -> main GEMM -> ...\r\n                \\-> dropout+dequant -> LoRA A GEMM -> ...\r\n```\r\nPrevious NVFP4 path:\r\n```\r\n-> RMSNorm -> quant -> main GEMM -> ...\r\n                   \\-> dequant -> dropout -> LoRA A GEMM -> ...\r\n```\r\nNew path for both FP8 and NVFP4:\r\n```\r\n-> RMSNorm -> quant -> main GEMM -> ...\r\n          \\-> dropout -> LoRA A GEMM -> ...\r\n```\r\n\r\n# Changelog\r\n\r\n- Stop pre-quantizing input to LoRA branch\r\n\r\n# GitHub Actions CI\r\n\r\nSee the [CI section](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#-running-github-ci) in the Contributing doc for how to trigger the CI. A Nvidia developer will need to approve and trigger the CI for external contributors.\r\n\r\n# Before your PR is \"Ready for review\"\r\n\r\n**Pre checks**:\r\n\r\n- [x] Make sure you read and followed [Contributor guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [ ] Did you write any new necessary tests?\r\n- [ ] Did you add or update any necessary documentation?\r\n- [x] Does the PR affect components that are optional to install? (Ex: Numba, Pynini, Apex etc)\r\n  - [ ] Reviewer: Does the PR have correct import guards for all optional libraries?\r\n\r\nIf you haven't finished some of the above items you can still open \"Draft\" PR.\r\n\r\n# Additional Information\r\n\r\n",
